#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:1
msgid "Finding the pages, and reading one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:3
msgid ""
"The first step is not writing a selection. It is finding out **how many "
"pages carry the datum**, and then reading one of them properly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:6
msgid "1. Find them"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:8
msgid ""
"`find-text` is the only command that works before the format knows "
"anything, because it searches the document rather than the format's idea "
"of it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:16
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`--text` is a substring and `--regex` is a regular expression, and they "
"are separate options because a {doc}`selection <../selections>` can never"
" be a regular expression. Searching with one and then carrying the "
"pattern into a selection is the usual first mistake."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:20
msgid "`--pages-only` prints `document:page`, which is what `inspect-page` takes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:22
msgid "2. Read the page as the engine reads it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:28
msgid ""
"`--mode lines` prints every line of the page with its font, its size and "
"its box, preceded by a legend naming each distinct *(font, size)* pair "
"once. It does **not** load the format, so it works on a format that does "
"not exist yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:32
msgid ""
"`--order x --columns 2` is worth typing by reflex. Many pages of these "
"reports carry **two tables side by side**, and the default top-to-bottom "
"order interleaves them into something unreadable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:35
msgid ""
"What you are looking for is the answer to one question: **what "
"distinguishes the thing you want from everything else on the page?** On a"
" holdings table it is usually the face. Here is one, and the whole "
"configuration that reads it follows from what this picture shows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:39
msgid ""
"A crop of a holdings table: a bold country heading, five lines of a "
"wrapped instrument name, and the figures level with its last line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:44
msgid "Three things, all of them decisions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:46
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**the body is `arialmt 8.5` and everything that is not body is `arial-"
"boldmt 8.5`** — the country heading `Germany (continued)`, the column "
"headings, the totals. A selection on the face alone therefore excludes "
"the headings, which is what keeps a format out of the commonest trap of "
"the `Collapse` cells ({doc}`parameters`);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:50
msgid ""
"**the instrument's name wraps over five lines**, and the figures sit "
"level with its **last** one. That is one cell, and which direction puts "
"it back together is read off this picture, not guessed;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:53
msgid ""
"**the superscript `1`** after `02/06/2035` is a footnote mark. In the "
"engine's line model it is a line of its own at 4.96 points, so a body "
"selection at 8.5 leaves it out without being told to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:56
msgid "3. Count the pages the anchor holds on"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:58
msgid "This is the step that is easy to skip and expensive to skip."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:60
msgid ""
"A classification anchor read off one page of `BLACKROCK-EN25` was "
"`Currency Holdings`, the column heading, which that page writes as one "
"text object. Measured over the document it covered **870** pages. The "
"heading `SCHEDULE OF INVESTMENTS` covered **1 063**. The 193-page gap was"
" not pages without a table: on **113** of them the same generator emitted"
" `Currency` and `Holdings` as **two** text objects, same table, same "
"columns, same everything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:66
msgid "A column heading reading \"Currency Holdings\" as a single run of text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:71
msgid ""
"The same heading on another page of the same document, with \"Currency\" "
"and \"Holdings\" set as two separate text objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:76
msgid ""
"The anchor that holds is `Investment`, the third column's heading: **983 "
"pages of 983**. The eighty pages of the schedule it leaves out are a "
"different table — forward currency contracts, and the per-sub-fund "
"summaries — and that was measured too, by searching those eighty pages "
"for every company the input database names and finding only the "
"umbrella's own name in the running head."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:81
msgid ""
"**Declaring an absence means saying what you searched for.** \"There is "
"nothing there\" is not a measurement; \"the seventy-six patterns of the "
"target list match nothing on those eighty pages except the running head\""
" is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:85
msgid "4. Then verify what varies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:87
msgid ""
"An anchor that holds on every page of one document is still only one "
"document. The property that makes a format worth writing is **constancy "
"inside the format**, so the next measurement is the same anchor over the "
"*other* reports of the same format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:91
msgid ""
"Where the format has only one report — a new issuer, a first year — that "
"measurement cannot be made, and the honest substitute is the one above: "
"every page of every class, with the number written down. Say which of the"
" two you did. A rule found on a single page has been propagated through a"
" status file, a plan and three documents before anybody looked at the "
"page after it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:96
msgid "The trap in the modes that follow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:98
msgid ""
"`inspect-page -m pdf_blks` shows what the first segment made of the page "
"and needs nothing. The other two are different:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/finding-and-reading.md:101
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**`-m txt_blks` and `-m results` need the right filter data, and that is "
"where an hour goes.** A `text_filter` that drops everything it cannot tie"
" to a fund of interest prints nothing when it is fed the wrong one, and "
"an empty printout looks exactly like a broken algorithm. The command "
"reads, in order, `--filter-data`, then the page type's own "
"`tests/formats/<FORMAT>/[<n>/]pages/<page type>/filter_data.json`, then "
"the target list — and it prints which one it used. If the line it prints "
"is not the fixture you meant, pass `--filter-data` rather than reading "
"the empty output as a result. {doc}`recipes-and-tests` is about building "
"one that proves something."
msgstr ""

